WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.167
This example combines a list, a function, and a tuple return value.

00:00:05.167 --> 00:00:09.507
Summarize_range receives a list of weekly sales.

00:00:09.507 --> 00:00:14.937
It finds the lowest value, the highest value, and the spread between them.

00:00:14.937 --> 00:00:18.802
Those three results are returned together as a tuple.

00:00:18.802 --> 00:00:24.682
For the current data, the low is thirty-nine hundred, the high is sixty-one hundred,

00:00:24.682 --> 00:00:26.746
and the range is twenty-two hundred.

00:00:27.436 --> 00:00:31.693
The caller then unpacks those results into three variables.

00:00:31.693 --> 00:00:35.963
This is a clean way to package several related summary values.
